<h3>Long-Term Value Analysis</h3>
<p>The extra ₹500–₹1,500 per sheet pays dividends over the furniture's lifespan. Precise hardware fit means hinges and drawer runners last longer without adjustment. Better surface consistency means laminates don't peel at edges due to substrate undulation. A kitchen built on calibrated boards is more likely to look new at year 7 than one built on standard stock.</p>
<h3>Return on Investment for Homeowners</h3>
<p>For a typical modular kitchen using approximately 40–55 sheets of 18 mm plywood, the calibration premium adds ₹20,000–₹55,000 to material cost — roughly 3–7% of an average modular kitchen project budget. Given that it directly impacts the quality of the most-used furniture in the home, this is one of the better value-per-rupee upgrades available.</p>
